# How buerligons reaches ClassCAD. The first of these that is set is used.

# 1. A ClassCAD worker (`classcad-cli worker`) over WebSocket: the default.
#    With it come session sharing and the invite panel: a page opened without
#    ?invite=<token> hosts a fresh session, one opened with it joins as a guest.
WSCLIENT_URL=ws://localhost:9094

# 2. ClassCAD in the browser (WASM): comment out 'WSCLIENT_URL' above.
#    The page then hosts its session itself. Its invites are joined where a ClassCAD MCP on the
#    same machine introduces the guests (an agent's session, or another page opened with the
#    invite link): ws://127.0.0.1:9098/session, or what CLASSCAD_SESSION_URL says.
#    The engine needs a key: put a public access token here (ccpk_…, made on
#    https://classcad.ch/account), and the key your plan allows is fetched for this page.
#    CLASSCAD_WASM_KEY takes a key of your own instead.
#CLASSCAD_TOKEN=ccpk_…

# 3. A ClassCAD server over SocketIO: comment out 'WSCLIENT_URL' above and leave 'CLASSCAD_TOKEN' unset.
SOCKETIO_URL=ws://localhost:9091

# Collaboration features (peer cameras, follow mode, cursors) are always on in
# shared sessions — no configuration needed or possible here.
